    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c05104f_7be4447e",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/fair.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3973,
      "author": {
        "id": 1456182
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-17T17:33:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was worried that might be a bit conservative.\n\nWe can improve the check so that we only ignore if\n\n    if (uclamp_min \u003e rq-\u003euclamp[UCLAMP_MAX].value)\n        return false;\n    \nRemoving it completely could make small tasks that needs boosting suffer?\n\nSomething else we might be able to do is check if the runtime of the task is smaller than the DVFS response time. If it\u0027ll go to sleep before DVFS can actually change the frequency, then generally the whole request could be useless. That can be a separate improvement to be done though. And it still seems risky in case this task only every once in a while performs something important that needs this boosting... Userspace being more intentional on when to set these values is the right approach. Kernel can\u0027t reason easiliy about it without the risk of breaking something.",
      "parentUuid": "04e0e250_0b35e525",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3971,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 3973,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "d356eedb7ba258936041277afed8e8507b6aa90f",
